# Secrets — never commit live keys
.env

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/

# Embedding/index caches (rebuilt automatically)
.tmp/

# Discover build output — Parquet views, regenerated by build_views.py from
# Data/ + the domain pack. The validation and profile reports under
# Insights/reports_prdw/ ARE committed; only the binaries are ignored.
Insights/views_prdw/
views_prdw/

# Office lock files
~$*


# WP-4 eval artefacts: regenerated by the harnesses, large, and meaningless
# without the run that produced them. The REPORT carries the numbers.
# The backend directory was Chatbot/ through WP-4c and is Ask/ since the tree
# was reorganised on 2026-08-18. Both spellings are listed: a rename that
# quietly un-ignores 200 MB of replay artefacts is the kind of thing that is
# noticed at `git add`, which is too late.
Ask/eval_full_results*.jsonl
Ask/eval_full_graded*.json
Ask/consistency_results.jsonl
Ask/consistency_table.csv
Chatbot/eval_full_results*.jsonl
Chatbot/eval_full_graded*.json
Chatbot/consistency_results.jsonl
Chatbot/consistency_table.csv
consistency_run.log

# Railway credentials — deploy/railway-deploy.sh reads the token from this file
# so it never has to be typed into a shell command, a chat window, or a commit.
deploy/.railway-token
*.railway-token

# The two Discover retrieval sidecars ARE COMMITTED (operator decision
# 2026-09-04, WP-D10 §8 option 1): the deployed `discover-api` has no volume
# and reads Insights/metainsights/ straight from git, and since WP-D10 the
# decompose half (74 MB .npy + 7 MB .json.gz) fits under GitHub's 100 MB
# per-file limit — committing it is what turns question decomposition ON in
# production. WP-D11 then grew the decompose matrix to 136.8 MB, over that
# limit, and WP-D11b (D61 ruling 1) SPLIT every vector matrix into stamped parts
# under 95 MB rather than shrink it. The committed files are now:
#   retrieval_corpus.json.gz / .part<N>.npy / _stamp.json
#   decompose_corpus.json.gz / .part<N>.npy / _stamp.json
# The stamps list every part with its SHA-256, and DiscoverChat's gate
# `vector-parts-under-limit` fails on a part over 100 MB or a stale file.
# Each mining rebuild re-commits ~150 MB; if mining becomes frequent, move the
# sidecars to a fetched artifact instead.
#
# The superseded spellings stay ignored, so a stale file left in a mirror
# cannot be committed by accident: the pre-D10 plain JSON, and the pre-D11b
# unsplit .npy (at decompose size it is over GitHub's limit and a push would be
# refused). NOTE: the two unsplit .npy files were TRACKED before WP-D11b, and an
# ignore line does not untrack a file -- the commit that adopts the split must
# record their deletion (`git rm --cached` is not needed: the files are gone
# from the working tree, so `git add -A` / `git rm` records it).
Insights/metainsights/retrieval_corpus.json
Insights/metainsights/decompose_corpus.json
retrieval_corpus.json
decompose_corpus.json
Insights/metainsights/retrieval_corpus.npy
Insights/metainsights/decompose_corpus.npy

# The resumable partial embedding cache phase5f writes while it runs, and
# removes when the build completes. Present only after a killed build.
Insights/metainsights/decompose_corpus.partial.npz
